# Exercise 3: AND
#
# A rule can need several things to be true at once. Put each goal on its
# own line, joining them with AND:
#
#     rule sibling_of_parent(x, y):
#         parent(p, y)
#         AND sibling(p, x)
#
# A variable that appears in two goals (p here) must be the same thing in
# both. That's how goals are connected.
#
# Your task: write grandparent(g, c), which is true when g is a parent of
# someone who is a parent of c.

fact parent("Ada", "Ben")
fact parent("Ada", "Fay")
fact parent("Ben", "Cy")
fact parent("Ben", "Di")
fact parent("Fay", "Eli")

# Write your rule below this line.



# --- Checks: run ./sova --check on this file. Don't change below here. ---
hint "You need two parent goals: g is a parent of someone, and that someone is a parent of c."
hint "Use a new variable for the person in the middle, for example m: parent(g, m) AND parent(m, c)."
expect grandparent("Ada", "Cy")
expect grandparent("Ada", "Eli")
expect NOT grandparent("Ben", "Cy")
expect NOT grandparent("Ada", "Ben")
expect grandparent("Ada", who) gives "Cy", "Di", "Eli"
expect grandparent(g, "Eli") gives "Ada"
